  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expand the Access to Effective and High Quality Health Services - Paraguay (01-Aug-2012-31-Jan-2016)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program supported by this grant aims to strengthen and improve the health system in Paraguay with activities aimed at tackling the weaknesses of the health system characterized, among other things, by inequitable access to health services, low coverage and an inefficient use of the available resources, including health products and personnel. Thanks to existing Global Fund-financed programs focused on TB and HIV, the services dealing with these diseases have improved, even if they are not completely coordinated with the general health system and in some aspect are affected by the weaknesses of the system. This grant will finance the full integration of these services, with a focus on prevention and the strengthening of primary health care. Additionally, special emphasis has been put on community outreach activities. The program targets the general population, with a concentration on pregnant women, young people and children; people living with HIV, people affected by TB and suspected TB cases; and health and community workers.</narrative>
  </description>
